&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;P: &amp;quot;though he lacked international experience&amp;quot; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;ndash; This part provides a contrasting detail and fits best at the end of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Q: &amp;quot;was selected for the Olympic squad&amp;quot; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;ndash; This part forms the main action and logically follows the subject.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R: &amp;quot;the young shooter&amp;quot; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;ndash; This part is the subject and should start the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;S: &amp;quot;due to his exceptional performance at the national trials&amp;quot; &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;ndash; This part explains the reason and fits after the action.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.&lt;br /&gt;
The update&lt;br /&gt;
P. ensuring security&lt;br /&gt;
Q. enhanced encryption&lt;br /&gt;
R. and data autonomy&lt;br /&gt;
S. across user devices&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 06 Aug 2025, Shift 1]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 2&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt; &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The given sentence needs to be rearranged to form a coherent and logical statement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct sequence is &lt;strong&gt;QRPS&lt;/strong&gt;, which forms the sentence: &lt;em&gt;"The update enhanced encryption, ensuring security and data autonomy across user devices."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Option 2 (QRPS) maintains the logical flow of the sentence: starting with the update's key feature (enhanced encryption), followed by its purpose (ensuring security), and then elaborating on the additional benefits (data autonomy across user devices).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 2&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt; &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rearranged Sentence:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;"The update enhanced encryption, ensuring security and data autonomy across user devices."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt; &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;P: "ensuring security"&lt;/strong&gt; – This part of the sentence indicates the purpose of the update.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Q: "enhanced encryption"&lt;/strong&gt; – This part highlights the primary feature of the update, and thus it should come first after the subject "The update."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R: "and data autonomy"&lt;/strong&gt; – This part adds more details about the benefits of the update.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;S: "across user devices"&lt;/strong&gt; – This part specifies where the benefits apply, making it the logical conclusion of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The economic slowdown&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;P. reducing consumer spending&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Q. in multiple industries&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;R. straining household incomes and&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;S. has led to job losses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 06 Aug 2025, Shift 1]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 2&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence describes the effects of an economic slowdown and how it has impacted various aspects of the economy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct order of the sentence should logically follow the sequence of cause and effect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct arrangement is &lt;strong&gt;SQRP&lt;/strong&gt;, as this sequence explains the economic slowdown leading to job losses, which strained household incomes, further reducing consumer spending in multiple industries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Option 2 is the correct answer as it provides a coherent and meaningful arrangement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 2&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correct Sentence:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;&amp;quot;The economic slowdown has led to job losses, straining household incomes and reducing consumer spending in multiple industries.&amp;quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;S: &amp;quot;has led to job losses,&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ndash; This part introduces the primary consequence of the economic slowdown.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;O: &amp;quot;straining household incomes and&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ndash; This part explains the further impact caused by job losses.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R: &amp;quot;reducing consumer spending&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ndash; This part highlights the effect on consumer behavior due to strained incomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;P: &amp;quot;in multiple industries.&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ndash; This part specifies the industries affected by reduced consumer spending.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Choose the correct sequence to form a meaningful sentence:&lt;br /&gt;
(A) is very interesting&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) Reading&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) books&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) fictional&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 06 Aug 2025, Shift 2]

solution.en:
&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is:&lt;strong&gt; BDCA&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B (Reading):&lt;/strong&gt; The subject of the sentence is the activity, &amp;quot;Reading.&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;D (fictional): &lt;/strong&gt;The adjective &amp;quot;fictional&amp;quot; directly describes the type of books being read.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C (books): &lt;/strong&gt;This is the object of the verb &amp;quot;reading,&amp;quot; referring to the material being read.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A (is very interesting): &lt;/strong&gt;This is the predicate, explaining the quality of the books being read.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So the correct sentence formed is: &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Reading fictional books is very interesting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (1)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;DABC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence begins with the subject &amp;quot;Everyone,&amp;quot; which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (D).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Following the subject, &amp;quot;should follow&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(DA)&lt;/strong&gt; continues the logical sequence, making it clear what everyone should do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The next part,&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;traffic rules&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(B)&lt;/strong&gt;, specifies what is being followed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ending with&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;strictly&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(C)&lt;/strong&gt; completes the sentence by emphasizing how the rules should be followed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;DABC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (DCAB):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;Everyone strictly should follow traffic rules,&amp;quot; which makes the sentence incorrect due to improper placement of the adverb &amp;quot;strictly.&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (DBCA):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;Everyone traffic rules should follow strictly,&amp;quot; which disrupts the logical sequence of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (DACB):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;Everyone should follow strictly traffic rules,&amp;quot; which is grammatically awkward and unclear.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (1)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;DBAC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;The sentence begins with the subject, &amp;quot;The manager,&amp;quot; which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (D).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Following the subject, &amp;quot;asked him&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(DB)&lt;/strong&gt; continues the logical flow, forming the action of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The next part,&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;to submit,&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(DBA)&lt;/strong&gt; specifies what the person is being asked to do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ending with&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;the report&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(DBAC) &lt;/strong&gt;completes the sentence by stating what the action is about.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;Correct sentence: The manager asked him to submit the report.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;DBAC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (BACD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;asked him to submit the manager,&amp;quot; which is grammatically incorrect and changes the intended meaning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (DBCA):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;The manager the report asked him to submit,&amp;quot; which disrupts the logical flow of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (DCAB):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;The manager to submit asked him the report,&amp;quot; which creates a fragmented and confusing sentence structure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rearrange the parts of this sentence:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) their demands&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) the workers&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) went on strike&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) after the management rejected&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 06 Aug 2025, Shift 3]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (3)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;BCDA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence begins with the subject &amp;quot;The workers,&amp;quot; which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (B).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Following the subject, &amp;quot;went on strike&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(BC)&lt;/strong&gt; continues the logical sequence, making it clear what the workers did.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The next part,&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;after the management rejected&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(BCD)&lt;/strong&gt; explains the reason for the strike.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ending with &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot;their demands&amp;quot; (BCDA) completes the sentence by stating what was rejected by the management.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;BCDA.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (DBAC):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;after the management rejected the workers went on strike,&amp;quot; which makes the sentence grammatically incorrect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (DACB):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;after the management rejected their demands the workers,&amp;quot; which disrupts the logical subject-verb-object flow.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (BACD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;the workers their demands went on strike after the management rejected,&amp;quot; which is confusing and grammatically incorrect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

