question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rearrange the parts of this sentence:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) despite poor rainfall&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) the farmers&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) managed to harvest&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) a good crop&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 06 Aug 2025, Shift 3]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (3)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;BACD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;The sentence begins with the subject &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;the farmers&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;quot; which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (B)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;The next part &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;despite poor rainfall&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; (A) provides the context for the farmers&amp;#39; actions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;This is followed by &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;managed to harvest&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; (C), which describes what the farmers did.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;The sentence ends with &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;a good crop&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; (D), completing the thought.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;BACD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (BDAC):&lt;/strong&gt; This arrangement creates an incorrect sequence as &amp;quot;despite poor rainfall&amp;quot; (A) cannot follow &amp;quot;the farmers&amp;quot; (B) directly without context.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (BADC):&lt;/strong&gt; This option places &amp;quot;a good crop&amp;quot; (D) before &amp;quot;managed to harvest&amp;quot; (C), disrupting the logical flow of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (CBAD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;managed to harvest&amp;quot; (C), which is incomplete without the preceding subject and context.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Choose the correct sequence to form a meaningful sentence:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) the guests&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) arrived&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) at the party&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) early&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 06 Aug 2025, Shift 3]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (2)&lt;/strong&gt;, i.e&lt;strong&gt;. ABDC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;The sentence begins with the action &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;the guests&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;quot; which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (A).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Following the action, &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;arrived,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(B)&lt;/strong&gt; continues the logical sequence, making it clear who arrived.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The next part,&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;early&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;quot; adds information about &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;when the guests arrived.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(D).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ending with&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;at the party,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt; (C) &lt;/strong&gt;completes the sentence by describing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;where the guests arrived.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bolder;"&gt;ABDC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1&amp;nbsp;(&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;BACD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;arrived &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;the guests&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;early at the party,&amp;quot; which is grammatically awkward and disrupts the natural flow of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (BADC):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;arrived the guests early at the party,&amp;quot; which is grammatically incorrect and does not make sense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (CBAD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;at the party arrived the guests early,&amp;quot; which creates a fragmented and confusing sentence structure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arrange the sentence parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) invited&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) to the event&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) many guests&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) were&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 06 Aug 2025, Shift 3]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 3&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;i.e. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;CDAB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The sentence begins with the subject &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;many guests&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;, correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (C)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The verb &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;were&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;part D&lt;/strong&gt;) follows the subject to form the basic structure of the sentence.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;invited&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;part A&lt;/strong&gt;) completes the predicate, indicating the action done to the subject.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The prepositional phrase &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;to the event&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;part B&lt;/strong&gt;) provides additional information about the action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;CDAB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (DABC):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because placing &amp;quot;invited&amp;quot; before &amp;quot;many guests&amp;quot; disrupts the subject-verb order.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (DCAB):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because &amp;quot;to the event&amp;quot; appears too early, making the sentence grammatically awkward.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4&amp;nbsp;(&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;DACB&lt;/span&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because the verb &amp;quot;were&amp;quot; comes after &amp;quot;many guests&amp;quot;. It can&amp;#39;t start with &amp;#39;were&amp;#39; hence it disturbs the&amp;nbsp;sentence flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arrange the sentence parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) after the meeting&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) the team members&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) went&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) to a restaurant&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 06 Aug 2025, Shift 3]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 4&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;BACD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The sentence begins with the subject &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;the team members&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;, correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (B)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The time phrase &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;after the meeting&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;part A&lt;/strong&gt;) is placed immediately after the subject to indicate when the action occurred.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The verb &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;went&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;part C&lt;/strong&gt;) follows the subject and time phrase to show the action.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The prepositional phrase &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;to a restaurant&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;part D&lt;/strong&gt;) indicates the destination, completing the sentence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;BACD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (ABCD):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because starting with &amp;quot;after the meeting&amp;quot; before the subject makes the sentence incomplete and awkward.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (BADC):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because placing the destination &amp;quot;to a restaurant&amp;quot; before the verb &amp;quot;went&amp;quot; disrupts natural sentence flow.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (BCAD):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because putting &amp;quot;after the meeting&amp;quot; after the verb &amp;quot;went&amp;quot; changes the standard placement of time phrases in English sentences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

