solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is&lt;strong&gt; Option (3)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;BACD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence begins with the subject &amp;quot;many passengers,&amp;quot; which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (B).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Following the subject, &amp;quot;were injured&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(BA)&lt;/strong&gt; continues the logical sequence, making it clear what happened to the passengers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The next part,&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;in the accident,&amp;quot; indicated by&lt;strong&gt; (C),&lt;/strong&gt; provides the context of the injury.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ending with &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot;yesterday&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(D)&lt;/strong&gt; completes the sentence by specifying the time.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;BACD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (BCAD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;many passengers in the accident were injured yesterday,&amp;quot; which breaks the logical flow and incorrectly structures the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (BCDA):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;many passengers in the accident yesterday were injured,&amp;quot; which places the time context too early in the sentence, disrupting coherence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (BADC):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;many passengers yesterday were injured in the accident,&amp;quot; which misplaces the time element, creating an awkward sentence structure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
