&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 07 Aug 2025, Shift 1]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (2)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;ACBD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence begins with the subject, &amp;quot;the winner,&amp;quot; which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (A).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Following the subject, &amp;quot;was declared&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(CB)&lt;/strong&gt; continues the logical sequence, making it clear what happened to the winner.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The final part,&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;yesterday&amp;quot; (ACBD) completes the sentence by providing the time reference.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bolder;"&gt;ACBD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;CABD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;was the winner declared&amp;nbsp;yesterday,&amp;quot; which makes the sentence grammatically incorrect and confusing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (BCAD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;declared was&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;&amp;nbsp;the winner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt; yesterday,&amp;quot; which disrupts the logical flow of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (CBAD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;was declared the winner yesterday,&amp;quot; which is not a coherent sequence for this context.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arrange the sentence parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) his advice&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) the students&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) accepted&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) happily&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 07 Aug 2025, Shift 1]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is&lt;strong&gt; Option (3)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;BCAD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence should start with the subject &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;the students&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (B).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Next, the verb &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;accepted&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (C) logically follows the subject.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Then comes the object &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;his advice&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (A), which is what was accepted.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Finally, the adverb &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;happily&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; (D) completes the sentence, showing the manner of acceptance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;BCAD&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (BACD):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because &amp;quot;the students his advice accepted happily&amp;quot; is not a grammatically valid order.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (BADC):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect as &amp;quot;the students advice happily accepted&amp;quot; misplaces the object and adverb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (ABCD):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because &amp;quot;his advice the students accepted happily&amp;quot; is awkward and not the most natural structure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arrange the sentence parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) by the end of the year&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) complete the new building&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) the construction company&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) promised to&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 07 Aug 2025, Shift 1]

solution.en:
&lt;p&gt;The correct order is &lt;strong&gt;CDBA&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s the correct reasoning:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;C starts with the subject: &amp;quot;The construction company.&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;D follows with the action: &amp;quot;promised to.&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;B continues the sentence with: &amp;quot;complete the new building&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;A finishes with: &amp;quot;by the end of the year.&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, the correct sequence is: &lt;strong&gt;C, D, B, A.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;This is a PYP question, and the official answer key has marked (correct option) as the correct answer, hence we cannot make any changes the options,&amp;nbsp;but we changed the solution with the actual right answer.&lt;/p&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Advances in satellite imaging&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;P. across diverse geographic regions&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Q. enabling accurate climate modelling&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;R. and disaster prediction systems&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;S. have transformed environmental monitoring,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 07 Aug 2025, Shift 2]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (1)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;SQRP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence begins with part &lt;strong&gt;(S)&lt;/strong&gt; as it introduces the subject, &amp;quot;Advances in satellite imaging have transformed environmental monitoring.&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The next part &lt;strong&gt;(Q)&lt;/strong&gt; logically continues the sentence with &amp;quot;enabling accurate climate modelling,&amp;quot; describing the purpose of these advances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Part &lt;strong&gt;(R)&lt;/strong&gt; follows next with &amp;quot;and disaster prediction systems,&amp;quot; adding further details about the applications of the advances.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Finally, part &lt;strong&gt;(P)&lt;/strong&gt; completes the sentence with &amp;quot;across diverse geographic regions,&amp;quot; explaining the scope of these applications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;SQRP.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (PRQS):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;across diverse geographic regions enabling accurate climate modelling,&amp;quot; which disrupts the logical flow of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (QPSR):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;enabling accurate climate modelling across diverse geographic regions,&amp;quot; which does not set the context properly as it skips the subject.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (RPSQ):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;and disaster prediction systems across diverse geographic regions,&amp;quot; which is incomplete and grammatically incorrect as the subject is missing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Choose the correct sequence to form a meaningful sentence:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) served&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) dinner&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) they&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) late&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 07 Aug 2025, Shift 2]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 4&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;To form a meaningful sentence, we must follow the correct grammatical order: &lt;strong&gt;Subject + Verb + Object + Adverb&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sentence C is the first part&lt;/strong&gt; as it provides the subject:&lt;/span&gt;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&amp;quot;they&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sentence A follows&lt;/strong&gt; as the verb:&lt;/span&gt;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&amp;quot;served&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sentence B comes next&lt;/strong&gt; as the object:&lt;/span&gt;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&amp;quot;dinner&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sentence D is the last part&lt;/strong&gt; as it adds additional information (adverb of time):&lt;/span&gt;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&amp;quot;late&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Thus, the correct sequence is &lt;strong&gt;CABD&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coherent sentence after rearrangement&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&amp;quot;They served dinner late.&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arrange the sentence parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) on time&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) the bus&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) arrived&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) at the stop&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 07 Aug 2025, Shift 2]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (1)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;BCAD&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The logical order of the sentence starts with the subject &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;the bus&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; &amp;ndash; indicated by &lt;strong&gt;(B)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Next comes the verb &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;arrived&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; &amp;ndash; indicated by &lt;strong&gt;(C)&lt;/strong&gt;, showing the action done by the bus.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The phrase&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bolder;"&gt;on time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;&amp;quot; &amp;ndash; indicated by&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bolder;"&gt;(A)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;, specifies when it happened.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Finally, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;indicated by&amp;nbsp;&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bolder;"&gt;at the stop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;&amp;quot; &amp;ndash;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bolder;"&gt;(D)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;, tells where the bus arrived.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&amp;nbsp;completing the sentence meaningfully.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;BCAD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (BACD):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because &amp;ldquo;the bus on time arrived at the stop&amp;rdquo; is grammatically wrong &amp;ndash; the adverbial phrase &amp;ldquo;on time&amp;rdquo; should come at the end.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (CBAD):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect as &amp;ldquo;arrived the bus on time at the stop&amp;rdquo; does not follow subject&amp;ndash;verb order.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (ABCD):&lt;/strong&gt; Incorrect because &amp;ldquo;on time the bus arrived at the stop&amp;rdquo; is awkward and not a natural English structure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arrange the sentence parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) announced&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) the winner&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) was&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) yesterday evening&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 07 Aug 2025, Shift 2]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (1)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;BCAD&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The logical order of sentence parts is determined by the subject, verb, and other sentence elements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Part &lt;strong&gt;(B)&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ldquo;the winner&amp;rdquo; serves as the subject of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Part &lt;strong&gt;(C)&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ldquo;was&amp;rdquo; acts as the helping verb connecting the subject to the action.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Part &lt;strong&gt;(A)&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ldquo;announced&amp;rdquo; is the main verb describing the action.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Part &lt;strong&gt;(D)&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;ldquo;yesterday evening&amp;rdquo; tells when the action took place and thus comes at the end.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Hence, the correct sequence is &lt;strong&gt;BCAD&lt;/strong&gt;, forming the sentence: &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;The winner was announced yesterday evening.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;BCAD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (CBAD):&lt;/strong&gt; Starts with a verb &amp;ldquo;was,&amp;rdquo; which makes the sentence incomplete at the beginning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (ACBD):&lt;/strong&gt; Begins with &amp;ldquo;announced,&amp;rdquo; which cannot start a meaningful sentence without a subject.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (BACD):&lt;/strong&gt; The structure &amp;ldquo;the winner announced was yesterday evening&amp;rdquo; is grammatically incorrect and illogical.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Arrange the sentence parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) met&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(B) his friend&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(C) at the station&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(D) Rohit&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 07 Aug 2025, Shift 3]

solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (4)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;DABC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;The sentence begins with the subject &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Rohit&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;, which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (D).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Following the subject, &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;met&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt; continues the logical sequence, making it clear what Rohit did, indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (A).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Next comes&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;his friend,&amp;quot; which provides more context to the sentence, indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (B).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finally,&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;at the station&amp;quot; completes the sentence by specifying the location, indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (C).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;DABC.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (DCBA):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;Rohit at the station his friend met,&amp;quot; which creates an incorrect and awkward sentence structure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (DBAC):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;Rohit his friend at the station met,&amp;quot; which disrupts the logical sequence of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (DACB):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;Rohit met at the station his friend,&amp;quot; which places the location before the object, making the sentence unclear.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rearrange the parts of this sentence:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(A) rising inflation&lt;/p&gt;

