solution.en:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (3)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;ABCD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt; &lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence begins with &lt;strong&gt;part (A)&lt;/strong&gt;, &amp;quot;rising inflation,&amp;quot; which is the subject of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Following the subject, &lt;strong&gt;part (B)&lt;/strong&gt;, &amp;quot;causes difficulties,&amp;quot; logically explains what rising inflation leads to.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Next, &lt;strong&gt;part (C)&lt;/strong&gt;, &amp;quot;for middle-class families,&amp;quot; specifies who faces these difficulties.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Finally, &lt;strong&gt;part (D)&lt;/strong&gt;, &amp;quot;everywhere,&amp;quot; concludes the sentence by indicating the universality of the problem.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;ABCD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt; &lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (BCAD):&lt;/strong&gt; This sequence starts with &amp;quot;causes difficulties rising inflation for middle-class families everywhere,&amp;quot; which disrupts the subject-verb agreement and logical flow.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (BACD):&lt;/strong&gt; This sequence begins with &amp;quot;rising inflation difficulties causes for middle-class families everywhere,&amp;quot; which is grammatically incorrect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 4 (BACD):&lt;/strong&gt; This is identical to Option 2 and therefore incorrect for the same reason.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
