	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Following the subject, &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;for higher education&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;(AC)&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;adds the purpose of the action, indicated by (A).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The next part,&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;prefer to go abroad&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;,&amp;quot;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;continues the logical sequence, indicating the action the students prefer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ending with &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot;these days&amp;quot; (D) completes the sentence by providing a time frame for the action.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;BACD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (ABCD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;for higher education many students these days prefer to go abroad,&amp;quot; which does not follow a logical sequence as the subject is not introduced first.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (BDAC):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;many students these days for higher education prefer to go abroad,&amp;quot; which creates an incomplete and awkward sentence structure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (BADC):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;many students for higher education these days prefer to go abroad,&amp;quot; which disrupts the flow of the sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

question.en:
