	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part (D):&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;before today&amp;quot; concludes the sentence with a time reference.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct arrangement is &lt;strong&gt;ABCD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (ACBD):&lt;/strong&gt; This arrangement disrupts the flow by placing &amp;quot;a huge gathering&amp;quot; before &amp;quot;seen such,&amp;quot; making the sentence awkward.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (ABDC):&lt;/strong&gt; This arrangement places &amp;quot;before today&amp;quot; prematurely, leading to a grammatically incorrect sentence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (BACD):&lt;/strong&gt; Starting with &amp;quot;seen such&amp;quot; misses the introductory subject &amp;quot;I have never,&amp;quot; breaking the logical sequence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
