question.en:
&lt;div&gt;Rearrange the parts of this sentence:&lt;br /&gt;
(A) the country&lt;br /&gt;
(B) was devastated&lt;br /&gt;
(C) by a powerful cyclone&lt;br /&gt;
(D) last month&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt; [Steno, 08 Aug 2025, Shift 3]

solution.en:
&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 1) ABCD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The sentence should start with the subject, followed by the verb, the object, and the time expression.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&amp;quot;The country&amp;quot; (A) is the subject, followed by the verb &amp;quot;was devastated&amp;quot; (B).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&amp;quot;By a powerful cyclone&amp;quot; (C) is the prepositional phrase explaining what caused the devastation, and &amp;quot;last month&amp;quot; (D) is the time expression, which logically comes at the end.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The correct arrangement is &amp;quot;The country was devastated by a powerful cyclone last month.&amp;quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is- ABCD.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Option 2) BACD starts with the verb, which would make the sentence less natural.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Option 3) ABDC disrupts the logical order of the sentence elements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Option 4) ACBD places the time expression too early, confusing the structure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (4)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;ABCD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence begins with the verb phrase &amp;quot;took care of,&amp;quot; which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (A).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Following the verb, the object of the action &amp;quot;her younger brother&amp;quot; is indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (B).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The next part, &amp;quot;while their parents,&amp;quot; adds the context for the action, which is indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (C).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Finally, &amp;quot;were away&amp;quot; completes the sentence and provides the necessary conclusion, indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (D).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct sequence is &lt;strong&gt;ABCD.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 1 (ACBD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option places &amp;quot;took care of&amp;quot; before &amp;quot;while their parents&amp;quot; without first introducing the object &amp;quot;her younger brother,&amp;quot; which disrupts the logical flow.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 2 (BACD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;her younger brother&amp;quot; before introducing the action &amp;quot;took care of,&amp;quot; which creates an unnatural sentence structure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Option 3 (CBAD):&lt;/strong&gt; This option starts with &amp;quot;while their parents&amp;quot; before introducing the main subject &amp;quot;she,&amp;quot; which is incorrect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Note:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;This is a PYP question, and the official answer key has marked (correct option) as the correct answer, hence we cannot make any changes to it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option (3)&lt;/strong&gt; i.e. &lt;strong&gt;ACBD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle; font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;The sentence begins with the subject &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;the cat&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;quot; which is correctly indicated by &lt;strong&gt;part (A).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Following the subject, &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;is&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; (C) connects the subject with the action, making the sentence grammatically correct.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;The next part &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;sleeping&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; (B) describes the action of the cat.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ending with &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;under the table&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; (D) provides the location, completing the sentence meaningfully.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

