&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;The word &lt;strong&gt;"Murmur"&lt;/strong&gt; is an example of onomatopoeia, which refers to words that imitate or resemble the sound they describe. (मर्मराहट)&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; The gentle murmur of the stream was soothing to the ears.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Onomatopoeia helps create a vivid sensory experience by mimicking actual sounds. (ध्वनि अनुकरण)&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Words like "buzz," "splash," and "whisper" are other examples of onomatopoeia.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is: &lt;strong&gt;Murmur&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here are the other options explained along with their Hindi meanings and example sentences:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Silence&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;चुप्पी&lt;/span&gt;): The absence of sound or noise.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; The room was filled with an eerie silence after the announcement.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Balloon&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;गुब्बारा&lt;/span&gt;): An inflatable object typically made of rubber.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; The children played joyfully with colorful balloons at the party.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Horrible&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;भयानक&lt;/span&gt;): Something extremely unpleasant or shocking.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Example:&lt;/strong&gt; The horrible storm caused widespread destruction in the town.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Q: Which of the following is an example of onomatopoeia?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is: &lt;b&gt;Murmur&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 2&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt; &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;The sentence "&lt;strong&gt;The old lady wept a river of tears&lt;/strong&gt;" uses an exaggerated expression to emphasize the extent of her sadness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;This is an example of &lt;strong&gt;Hyperbole&lt;/strong&gt;, a figure of speech that uses deliberate and obvious exaggeration for dramatic effect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Hyperbole is often used to evoke strong feelings or create a vivid mental image.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;In this case, the expression "a river of tears" is not literal but exaggerates the old lady’s intense emotions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 2&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt; &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explanation:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;The sentence does not employ euphemism, alliteration, or anticlimax, as these figures of speech serve different purposes. Instead, the vivid exaggeration aligns with hyperbole.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt; &lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Euphemism:&lt;/strong&gt; A mild or indirect word/expression used to substitute something harsh or blunt (e.g., "passed away" for "died").&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alliteration:&lt;/strong&gt; The repetition of the same initial consonant sound in closely connected words (e.g., "She sells seashells by the seashore").&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anticlimax:&lt;/strong&gt; A sudden transition from a significant idea to a trivial one for humorous or ironic effect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hyperbole:&lt;/strong&gt; An exaggerated statement not meant to be taken literally, often used for emphasis or effect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&lt;strong&gt; Option 2.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;The line "I wandered lonely as a cloud" is an example of a simile.&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;A simile is a figure of speech that compares two different things using "like" or "as."&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;In this case, the poet compares his wandering to a lonely cloud, emphasizing the sense of isolation and movement.&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;This line is from William Wordsworth's poem "Daffodils," which explores themes of nature, beauty, and reflection.&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;Wordsworth often used vivid imagery and figures of speech to evoke emotions and connect readers to the natural world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"&gt;Therefore, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 2.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;"&gt;&lt;img height="26px" src="https://cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png" width="26px"  style="width: 28px !important; height: 28px !important; display: inline-block !important; vertical-align: middle !important; margin: 0 8px 0 0 !important;" /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hyperbole:&lt;/strong&gt; An exaggerated statement or claim not meant to be taken literally.&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Metaphor:&lt;/strong&gt; A figure of speech that directly compares two unlike things without using "like" or "as."&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personification:&lt;/strong&gt; Assigning human traits or qualities to non-human entities or objects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
